### Fleuréa Petals API — request tests
### Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or Visual Studio and send each request.
### Base URL of the running ASP.NET Core API.

@base = https://localhost:7043/api/v1
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_JWT_HERE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CATALOGUE  (public)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### List active categories
GET {{base}}/categories

### List products — everlasting only, page 1
GET {{base}}/products?nature=everlasting&page=1&pageSize=12

### Search products
GET {{base}}/products?search=ribbon

### Product detail
GET {{base}}/products/rosewood-ribbon-bouquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORDERING  (public)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Place an order  ->  calls fn_place_order in PostgreSQL
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": 2, "quantity": 2 }
  ],
  "contact":  { "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012" },
  "delivery": {
    "recipientName": "Beena Parmar", "phone": "9800000012",
    "line1": "14, Rose Villa, Linking Road", "line2": "",
    "city": "Mumbai", "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400052", "landmark": "",
    "date": "2026-09-12", "slot": "morning"
  },
  "giftMessage": "Happy birthday, Ma.",
  "customerNote": ""
}

### Negative test — empty cart (expect 400 EMPTY_ORDER)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [], "contact": { "name": "X", "email": "x@x.com", "phone": "0" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "X", "phone": "0", "line1": "a", "line2": "", "city": "Mumbai",
    "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400001", "landmark": "", "date": "2026-09-12", "slot": "morning" } }

### Negative test — delivery date too soon for a made-to-order item (expect 400 DELIVERY_TOO_SOON)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [ { "productId": 3, "quantity": 1 } ],
  "contact":  { "name": "Test", "email": "test@example.com", "phone": "9999999999" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "Test", "phone": "9999999999", "line1": "1 A Road", "line2": "",
    "city": "Mumbai", "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400001", "landmark": "",
    "date": "2026-01-01", "slot": "evening" }
}

### Track an order (guest)
GET {{base}}/orders/FP-2026-000042?email=beena.parmar@example.com

### Track — wrong e-mail (expect 404 / access denied)
GET {{base}}/orders/FP-2026-000042?email=someone.else@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUSTOM REQUESTS  (public)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Submit a custom bouquet request
POST {{base}}/custom-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contactName": "Ronak Parmar", "contactEmail": "ronak.parmar@example.com", "contactPhone": "9700000040",
  "bouquetType": "mixed", "occasion": "25th wedding anniversary",
  "palette": "Ivory, blush, a little gold", "flowersPreferred": "Roses and lisianthus",
  "size": "large", "budgetMin": 2500, "budgetMax": 4000,
  "needByDate": "2026-10-02", "referenceNotes": "Photographs well on a dinner table.",
  "inspirationImageUrl": null
}

### Track a custom request
GET {{base}}/custom-requests/FP-CR-2026-000007?email=ronak.parmar@example.com

### Footer enquiry
POST {{base}}/enquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Priya N", "email": "priya@example.com", "message": "Do you deliver to Thane?" }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUSTOMER ACCOUNT  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012", "password": "petals-secret" }

### Login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "password": "petals-secret" }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMIN  (requires admin JWT — log in as "forum")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Admin login  (seeded account: username "forum")
POST {{base}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "forum", "password": "petals123" }

### Dashboard summary  ->  fn_dashboard_summary()
GET {{base}}/admin/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List pending orders
GET {{base}}/admin/orders?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Advance an order's status  ->  fn_update_order_status(...)
PUT {{base}}/admin/orders/42/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "confirmed" }

### Respond to a custom request  ->  fn_respond_custom_request(...)
PUT {{base}}/admin/custom-requests/7
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "quoted", "adminResponse": "Two options attached, both within budget.", "quotedPrice": 3400 }

### Create a product  ->  fn_upsert_product(...)
POST {{base}}/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1, "name": "Ivory & Gold Ribbon Spray", "slug": "ivory-gold-ribbon-spray",
  "shortDescription": "Ivory ribbon roses with fine gold thread.", "description": "...",
  "nature": "everlasting", "price": 1650, "isCustomizable": true,
  "availability": "available", "leadTimeDays": 4, "isActive": true
}

### Toggle availability  ->  fn_set_product_availability(...)
PUT {{base}}/admin/products/6/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "availability": "sold_out" }

# ===========================================================================
# NEGATIVE & EDGE CASES  (expected to fail — that is the point)
# ===========================================================================

### N1  Search with no matches -> 200 with an empty list, not an error
GET {{base}}/products?search=xylophone

### N2  Unknown product slug -> 404
GET {{base}}/products/does-not-exist

### N3  Order a sold-out product -> 400  PRODUCT_SOLD_OUT
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": 6, "quantity": 1 } ],
  "contact": { "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "Beena Parmar", "phone": "9800000012", "line1": "14 Rose Villa", "line2": "",
    "city": "Mumbai", "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400052", "landmark": "",
    "date": "2026-12-01", "slot": "morning" } }

### N4  Fresh item ordered for same day -> 400  DELIVERY_TOO_SOON
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": 4, "quantity": 1 } ],
  "contact": { "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "Beena Parmar", "phone": "9800000012", "line1": "14 Rose Villa", "line2": "",
    "city": "Mumbai", "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400052", "landmark": "",
    "date": "2026-09-09", "slot": "morning" } }

### N5  Client sends its own price -> ignored; order total uses catalogue price
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1, "price": 1 } ],
  "contact": { "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "Beena Parmar", "phone": "9800000012", "line1": "14 Rose Villa", "line2": "",
    "city": "Mumbai", "state": "Maharashtra", "postalCode": "400052", "landmark": "",
    "date": "2026-09-20", "slot": "morning" } }

### N6  Checkout with missing required fields -> 400 with field errors
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ], "contact": { "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "phone": "" },
  "delivery": { "recipientName": "", "phone": "", "line1": "", "line2": "", "city": "", "state": "",
    "postalCode": "", "landmark": "", "date": null, "slot": "midnight" } }

### N7  Track an order with the wrong e-mail -> 404 / access denied
GET {{base}}/orders/FP-2026-000042?email=someone.else@example.com

### N8  Register with an e-mail that already has an account -> 409  EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Beena Parmar", "email": "beena.parmar@example.com", "phone": "9800000012", "password": "another" }

### N9  Admin login with a wrong password -> 401
POST {{base}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "forum", "password": "wrong" }

### N10  Admin endpoint without a token -> 401
GET {{base}}/admin/orders

### N11  Invalid order status transition (skip / go backwards) -> 409  INVALID_TRANSITION
PUT {{base}}/admin/orders/42/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "pending" }

### N12  Cancel an order that is already out for delivery -> 409  CANNOT_CANCEL
PUT {{base}}/admin/orders/40/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled" }

### N13  Custom request missing the required "need by" date -> 400
POST {{base}}/custom-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactName": "Ronak Parmar", "contactEmail": "ronak.parmar@example.com", "contactPhone": "9700000040",
  "bouquetType": "ribbon", "occasion": "Birthday", "size": "standard" }
